Here's a possible implementation of a C++ function that converts Markdown to HTML using the popular Markdown library called "pugixml":

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <pugixml.hpp>

// Function to convert Markdown to HTML
std::string markdown_to_html(const std::string& markdown) {
    // Create a pugi XML document
    pugi::xml_document doc;
    pugi::xml_parse_result result = doc.load_string(markdown.c_str());

    // Check for parsing errors
    if (!result) {
        std::cerr << "Error parsing Markdown: " << result.description() << std::endl;
        return "";
    }

    // Load the Markdown into a pugi XML element
    pugi::xml_node root = doc.first_child();

    // Convert Markdown to HTML using pugixml
    std::stringstream html_stream;
    pugi::xml_node converted_node = pugi::create_from_string("<html><body>", "UTF-8");
    pugi::xml_node converted_body_node = converted_node.append_child("body");
    pugi::xml_node converted_root_node = converted_body_node.append_child(pugi::node_element);
    converted_root_node.append_copy(root);
    pugi::xml_save_file(converted_node, html_stream);

    // Remove unnecessary HTML tags
    std::string html = html_stream.str();
    html.erase(html.find_last_of("<body>") + 6);
    html.erase(0, html.find_first_of("</body>") + 9);
    html.erase(html.find_last_of("</html>") + 8);

    return html;
}

int main() {
    std::string markdown = "Hello **world**! This is a *test*.";
    std::string html = markdown_to_html(markdown);
    std::cout << html << std::endl;
    return 0;
}
```

This function first loads the Markdown text into a pugi XML document using the `load_string` method. It then creates a new XML document with an HTML structure using `create_from_string`, and uses `append_copy` to insert the Markdown content inside the body element. Finally, it saves the converted XML to a stringstream, removes unnecessary HTML tags, and returns the resulting HTML string.

Note that this implementation uses pugixml, which is a third-party library. You may need to install it first before compiling this code. Also, this implementation only handles a basic subset of Markdown syntax. For more advanced features, you may need to use a more complete Markdown library or a dedicated Markdown-to-HTML converter.

